Wiz-Elf-Mal-Cha
artiwishless, polyselfless, polypileless

This is the final ascension in my alphabetic ascension series. Seven
games were required to win. This might have probably been 6 if it
weren't for a stupid cockatrice death at Vlad's Tower. It might even
be continuation of my streak, if I didn't get killed unluckily on my
first wizard game by a unicorn summoned by nymph in distress. This
game is my fastest game-time and real-time ascension (27807 turns,
14:47).

Here's my game:

1) In starting room there are a potion, a scroll, Vorpal Sword (right
next to me) and +1 gauntlets of power. That's ridiculously lucky
beginning, since Vorpal Blade lasted me till I got Magicbane.

2) There were coaligned altars at dlvl 3 and 8. The latter was in the
same room as upstairs to Sokoban, making stashing stuff there even
more convenient. There were two other coaligned temples deeper in the
dungeon and that one crossaligned altar I converted to chaotic.
Another exteremly lucky circumstances in this game.

3) I did Sokoban first, got amulet of reflection.

4) After rather lot of sacrificing I finally got my Magicbane so I
could switch from Vorpal Blade (which didn't train any skill for me).

5) At Minetown I got bag of holding and magic lamp; dumping my gold at
crossaligned temple netted me 5 points

6) This game saw five bone levels, including dlvl 11 bones of ranger
cstaub67 with three magic markers, tinning kit, magic whistle, bag of
holding (not needed at this point) and speed boots. Another stroke of
luck.

7) At dlvl 12 I got graveyard with good number of wraiths and nearby
upstairs. I went from XL 12 to XL 16 easily.

8) At dlvl 14 there was coaligned temple, where I got crowned.

9) I used one of my magic lamps to get silver dragon scale mail, so I
could put on my amulet of ESP. And also get rid of mithril mail so I
could actually spellcast.

10) For the first time I could embark on my Quest right after reaching
the portal level.

11) At dlvl 20 I got genocide and a wish from a throne. I genocided
disenchanters and wished for ring of free action.

12) Before I got to the Castle I already was powerful wizard, with
finger of death at 0% failure rate, magic mapping, detect monsters,
magic missile etc.

13) Castle was completely uneventful (well, except getting sandwiched
beween to master liches on arrival), I didn't use the wand of wishing
at all, I just put it away for later use.

14) Before entering VoTD, I used my magic markers (I already had
_five_ of them) to up my AC to -35, echant my Magicbane to +7 and
acquire purple worm pet. I also wrote spellbook of dig, and scroll of
charging.

15) Cleared VoTD while seeing to it that my purple worm gets all the
wraiths. After we cleared VoTD, it was over 300 maxHP and XL 45.

16) With magic mapping and digging spell, Gehennom was a breeze. Vlad
was instakilled by my purple worm, which by this brave deed earned its
nickname: Vladsbane.

17) After reaching VS level and finding vibrating square I
branchported to my stash at Sokoban and made final preparations, which
included wishing for a stethoscope. My main worry was that I don't
have any means of confusing myself. I hoped that by reaching the
Planes I will forget some spell. That did not happen. My maxHP at this
point was some 150. It would feel very inadequate for any other role,
but wizard is so powerful in late game, that I didn't feel need for
any more upgrade.

18) I quickly reached the Wizard, killed him with finger of death,
levelported to VS level, performed the ritual and levelported to the
Moloch's Sanctum.

19) Moloch's Sanctum was tense. Levelport didn't buy me much advantage
and I had to make almost complete circle around the Temple of Moloch.
Vladsbane the purple worm promptly swallowed the high priest and we
got out together.

20) Run to the Planes was uneventful with three (I think) Rodney
visitations.

21) On the Planes, I had to find a way to find end game portals. I
still had no means of confusing myself. But I recalled, that reading
cursed scroll of confuse monster will actually confuse the player
reading it. So I cursed my stack of 4 unlabelled scrolls with the only
left potion of unholy water and wrote confuse monster. It worked
perfectly. The Planes were easy going. On the plane of Air I had to
zap wand of death (I had two) at three engulfing air elementals. And
oh, I forgot to call my Vladsbane the purple worm when I was entering
the portal at the Plane of Fire. Exactly the same stupid mistake I did
on my very first ascension, when I left my pet purple worm Bianca at
the Plane of Air.

22) At the Astral Plane, I used the 0:1 wish from the Castle wand to
get rubber chicken, which lasted me till the end of the game. I didn't
use conflict, instead I put on ring of regeneration halfway through.
The second altar was the correct one.

Overall, I can say that I can see why people play wizards so much. The
possibility of getting great rings, spells and scrolls in the
beginning, and the sheer variability of the gameplay make them really
interesting and the late game is extremely powerful compared to other
roles.

